<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>HCMv3 DevExpress Report Designer -- rptPayslipEn</title>
    <style>
        html, body { height: 100%; margin: 0; font-family: Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif; }
    </style>
    @*
      UseDevExpressControls()/RenderScripts() emit the widget CONTAINER + init call, but not the
      underlying DevExtreme/devexpress-reporting JS libraries themselves. Three things were tried:
        (a) CDN <script>/<link> tags for everything (https://cdn3.devexpress.com/jslib/23.2.13/...) --
            dx.all.js/dx.light.css ARE published there (200), but dx-analytics-core.min.js and
            dx-reportdesigner.min.js 403 (AccessDenied) at every version tried -- the Reporting-specific
            bundles simply are not on that public CDN.
        (b) Html.DevExpress().StyleSheets()/.Scripts() + ApplicationOptions.UseIntegratedClientSideResources
            (DevExpress's own embedded-resource middleware, served at /DXR.axd) -- builds and starts,
            but every /DXR.axd request 500s with no exception surfacing anywhere (not even through a
            custom exception-logging middleware wrapped around it), so this mode could not be debugged
            further in the time available.
        (c) What's used below: `npm install devextreme@23.2.13 devexpress-reporting@23.2.13 jquery
            knockout` (see package.json) and copy the prebuilt dist/ bundles into wwwroot/lib -- the
            same files the demo project's webpack build ultimately produces, minus webpack. dx.all.js /
            dx.light.css still come from the CDN since that half genuinely works; only the
            Reporting-specific pieces are local.
    *@
    <link href="https://cdn3.devexpress.com/jslib/23.2.13/css/dx.light.css" rel="stylesheet" />
    <script src="~/lib/jquery.min.js"></script>
    <script src="~/lib/knockout-latest.js"></script>
    <!-- DevExtreme must load AFTER Knockout ("The DevExtreme library is included before the Knockout
         library" console error otherwise) and jQuery must come first for the reporting widgets' DOM code. -->
    <script src="https://cdn3.devexpress.com/jslib/23.2.13/js/dx.all.js"></script>
    <link href="~/lib/dx-analytics.light.css" rel="stylesheet" />
    <script src="~/lib/dx-analytics-core.min.js"></script>
    <script src="~/lib/dx-querybuilder.min.js"></script>
    <!-- The Report Designer bundle assumes the Web Document Viewer bundle (DevExpress.Reporting.*)
         has already run -- Designer = Viewer + authoring UI, not a standalone superset script. -->
    <link href="~/lib/dx-webdocumentviewer.css" rel="stylesheet" />
    <script src="~/lib/dx-webdocumentviewer.min.js"></script>
    <link href="~/lib/dx-reportdesigner.css" rel="stylesheet" />
    <link href="~/lib/dx-reporting-skeleton-screen.css" rel="stylesheet" />
    <script src="~/lib/dx-reportdesigner.min.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
    @RenderBody()
    @RenderSection("Scripts", required: false)
</body>
</html>
